            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new run of words: what did zyādā mean, and what did kam mean?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: मेहरबानी",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मेहरबानी (mehrabānī) — \"kindness\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Persian mihrbān, 'kind', with the quality-ending on the back of it. Under mihrbān is mihr, an old Iranian word for love and for the sun, and the god Mithra before either."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two words in your Hindi now begin meh- and are not related at all: मेहमान, the guest, is Persian mihmān, a different word entirely. Same opening syllable in our letters, separate families."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The first of five words for asking well."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "mehrabānī",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *mehrabānī*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "it once more, slowly",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: it once more, slowly]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "mehrabānī, then mehmān, and say which one is the guest",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *mehrabānī*, then *mehmān*, and say which one is the guest]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
