          "title": "You'll want to know: अनुमति",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अनुमति (anumati) — \"permission\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Sanskrit, and transparent: अनु (anu), 'along with, after', plus मति (mati), 'thought'. Permission is thinking along with someone — agreeing in mind before agreeing in words."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It is the formal one. On a form, at a desk, or in front of anyone whose yes carries weight, अनुमति (anumati) is the word; among friends nobody says it. Hindi keeps a Sanskrit word in reserve for exactly these rooms."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
