              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "भरोसा (bharosā) — \"trust\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Usually built on भर (bhara), 'a load, a support', from the root भृ (bhṛ-), 'to bear, to carry'. Trust is named as the thing that takes your weight."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "That picture runs through the way the word is said, too: a speaker puts भरोसा (bharosā) on someone rather than in them. The load goes on top, and the person underneath either holds or does not."
            }
          ]
        },
