        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: अदब",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अदब (adab) — \"good manners\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Arabic adab, and here is the surprise: the same word means literature. Courtesy and letters were one idea — the cultivation that makes a person fit company, whether it shows in a bow or on a page."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Guard it against आदर, which you already own. ādar is respect you feel and show upward; adab is the whole trained manner a person carries. Close in our letters, and not the same word."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Five: मेहरबानी (mehrabānī), विनती (vintī), अनुमति (anumati), भरोसा (bharosā), अदब (adab). Enough to ask for a thing at the weight the room asks for."
            }
          ]
        },
